Package: imp72
Architecture: amd64 arm64 mips64el
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, gcc | c-compiler
Description: IMP72 systems programming language compiler
 IMP72 is the extensible systems language of Ned Irons, in the compiler
 Walter Bilofsky wrote for the PDP-10 (DECUS 10-198a, 1973): a small kernel
 reads the syntax and semantics of the language from a file in its own
 notation.  This is a port of that compiler to 64 bit machines, keeping the
 original syntax file and code generator.
 .
 imp72c compiles IMP72 programs to native code and links them with a small
 runtime.  A subroutine is a C function (arguments by reference, as in
 FORTRAN), and CCALL calls C functions with arguments by value.  The code
 generator is the pcc compiler's pass 2 on amd64; on every other machine the
 program is turned into C for the system compiler.
 .
 Only 64 bit little endian machines are supported: the language's word is 64
 bits and strings are packed little endian.
